  "id": "Compound::DB01181 - Disease::DOID:2531",
  "verbalization": "Ifosfamide is linked to Hematologic Cancer through a series of indirect pathways that converge on the disease. The evidence suggests that Ifosfamide causes Frank Hematuria, which is then linked to Alitretinoin, a compound that treats Hematologic Cancer. Similarly, Ifosfamide causes Congestive Cardiomyopathy, which is associated with Dasatinib, another agent that treats Hematologic Cancer. Lastly, Ifosfamide leads to Premature Menopause, caused by Doxorubicin, which also targets Hematologic Cancer. These pathways all share a common link to Antineoplastic Agents and Heteroorganic Entities, suggesting a broader class of compounds that may exert antitumor effects. The integration of these mechanisms highlights the potential of Ifosfamide as a candidate for repurposing in Hematologic Cancer, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
